title: The Chair and the Agenda
subtitle: Whoever writes the agenda writes half the resolution.
view-if: congress = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and congress_used_procedure = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.congress_used_procedure = 1;
!}
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= The Chair and the Agenda

The presidium of the congress meets before breakfast to settle the order of business. Our people hold the chair. [? if congress_ahead = 1 : We are ahead, for now. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 : We are behind, for now. ?]

- @first: Put our motion first on the agenda.
- @close: Move the closure of the debate.
- @adjourn: Adjourn for a night of caucusing.

@first
subtitle: A small edge: the first motion sets the terms of the debate.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway(0.03);
!}

Our motion comes first. Every other speaker has to answer it. Our side now has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@close
subtitle: The vote comes after this session, while we are ahead. The losers will call it a manoeuvre.
view-if: congress_ahead = 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.closeEarly();
RG.congress.bitter(2);
!}

The chair puts the closure to the vote, and carries it. There will be no more speeches: the congress votes when this session ends.

@adjourn
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. One more session before the vote.
choose-if: resources >= 1 and congress_sessions < 6
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds to keep the delegates in Berlin.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
RG.congress.extend(1);
!}

The congress adjourns until tomorrow. The delegates' hotels are paid for one more night, and nobody sleeps much.
